Three fixes the FEX-2607 rebase exposed for running x86-64 guests on iOS:

- loader.c load_arm64ec_module (Phase 1.5): walk_node_dependencies() →
  process_attach() so xtajit64's OWN DllMain runs (mingw _DllMainCRTStartup →
  _initterm → C++ constructors). walk_node_dependencies attaches only a node's
  deps, never the node itself; on iOS FEX's InitCRTProcess is a no-op and relies
  on mingw's DllMain, so its ctors never ran → libc++'s lazily-resolved
  GetSystemTimePreciseAsFileTime ptr stayed null → first system_clock::now()
  dispatched an indirect call to 0 (fault in #arm64x_check_call, x11=0). This is
  THE cube-x64 render fix. Idempotent (early-outs LDR_PROCESS_ATTACHED); non-iOS
  harmless (xtajit64 DllMain is a stub, ctors run via CRT.cpp InitCRTProcess).

- loader.c loader_init: hoist locale_init() to just before load_arm64ec_module()
  inside the __arm64ec__ block. The rebased xtajit64 arm64ec_process_init now
  uppercases (RtlUpcase… → reads the NLS casemap) BEFORE stock locale_init()
  wires it ~15 lines below → NULL upcase table → cube white-screen livelock.
  Safe: locale_init's only actctx dep fails gracefully; it re-runs later.

- unix_private.h is_ec_code: on iOS use THIS thread's peb via
  pthread_getspecific(teb_key) (reliable when x18=0) instead of the global `peb`,
  which drifts across co-resident pseudo-processes — a cube worker thread was
  reading a sibling process's null EcCodeBitMap and faulting in context restore.

(cherry picked from commit 6c7286a6134ae4bb052dda5ac310cb3dacee0c1b)
